course: dictionary
lesson: 5535
title: Leftover and what it can mean
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. «Her first dish is bubble-and-squeak, made from fried leftover cabbage and potato.» Fried cabbage and potato that is cooked again after a meal is leftover food.
explain: Leftover can also describe a thing, as an adjective. «Leftover paint» and «leftover money» are paint and money that were not used. In maths, «24 sweets shared among 5 children: each gets 4, and 4 are left over» means the sweets that are not shared out. Here leftover means the remainder.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a word like «spare» or «not used» and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Leftover can mean food that is not eaten at a meal and is kept for later.
fact: As an adjective, leftover means remaining or not used, as in «leftover paint».
fact: Keep leftovers in a fridge kept below about 5 degrees, and eat them within a day or two.
fact: Heat leftovers until they are piping hot before you eat them.
fact: Cutting food waste is part of caring for the planet.
exercise: «Fish should get only as much food as they eat in a couple of minutes, because leftovers rot and poison the water.» What are leftovers in this sentence? | *Food that is not eaten and rots in the water | Fish that swim away from the pond | Fresh food, just caught | Stones from the bottom of the pond
exercise: «Leftover paint» is in a painting lesson. What does leftover mean here? | Very large | Wet and sticky | *Remaining, not used | Brand new
exercise: «24 sweets shared among 5 children: each gets 4, and 4 are left over.» In maths, what are the 4 left over? | Sweets that are sticky | Four extra children | *The remainder, not shared out | The total number of sweets
test: «Food stays safer in a fridge kept below about 5 degrees, because germs grow slowly in the cold, so leftovers go in once they have cooled.» Why do leftovers go in the fridge once they have cooled? | Leftovers must be eaten straight away | *Germs grow slowly in the cold | Hot food is tastier when cold | Fridges need warm food to work
test: «A real fox eats rabbits, mice, birds, worms, beetles, fruit and leftovers, so food chains join into a tangled food web.» Why does this help animals? | *They can switch food when one food runs short | Food webs are only made of rabbits | Foxes eat only fruit | Animals never eat leftovers
exam: «Leftover bread makes the water dirty and attracts rats.» What does this tell you about feeding ducks leftover bread? | *It is not good for ducks or the pond | It keeps rats away from the pond | It is the best food for ducks | Ducks need it every day
